{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"kinetic-dewy-reindeer","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\nADR 0123 §6 (`docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md`, the \"Pipeline-only steps\" bullet) says of the pre-dispatch shortcuts: \"Each reuses or re-signs a pipeline attestation or verdict\", and its \"Why\" list says \"The shortcuts hand back a pipeline attestation or verdict\". That is wrong for 2 of the 3 shortcuts.\n\n`reuse.idempotent_reuse` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py`) is gated by `claim_gate_check` alone, so a pipeline review on a ticket whose current attestation was signed by the **agentic** engine returns the reused PASS (`coverage.idempotent_skip: true`, `runner: \"reused\"`) without running the pipeline. `orchestrator.drift_refresh` likewise re-signs the prior attestation and carries its engine forward (`attest.py`: \"A refresh re-binds the PRIOR verdict, so its engine is still the provenance\"). Only `reuse.verdict_reuse` is engine-matched (it refuses a sidecar whose `coverage.engine` is not `pipeline`).\n\nThat engine-agnostic reuse is the intended design: story `confident-snooty-stinkpot` records it (\"a pipeline run on an agentic-certified ticket reports `idempotent_skip`\"), and `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py::test_an_agentic_pass_certifies_for_a_later_pipeline_review` pins it. The ADR text, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing the engine\", which says only that a pipeline run and an agentic run are \"separate jobs\", do not tell a reader that an explicit `engine=pipeline` request can return the agentic result.\n\nObserved on production (aa1681bb531, 2026-11-13 09:19 PST): `review_plan_start` with `engine: \"pipeline\"` on `brocatello-industrial-leafbird`, which held a current agentic attestation, finished with `decided_by_run: false`, the replayed agentic `REVIEW_RESULT`, the unchanged `signed_at`, and `plan_review_status` still reporting `engine: \"agentic\"`. The same reproduces locally with `rebar review-plan <id> --engine pipeline`, which returned `runner: \"reused\"` in 2 s.\n\nA smaller, related gap: the MCP `plan_review_status` tool description (`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`) lists its return as `{ok, verdict, reason, verified_at_sha, signed_at}`, but it also returns `currency_basis` and `engine` (`attest_gate.plan_review_status`), and `engine` is part of ADR 0123 §5's contract.\n\n## Approach\nCorrect the documentation to match the pinned behaviour. Do not change behaviour.\n- ADR 0123 §6: state that `verdict_reuse` replays only a pipeline BLOCK, while `idempotent_reuse` and `drift_refresh` act on the current attestation whichever engine signed it, so a pipeline request on an agentic-certified, unchanged ticket returns the reused agentic PASS, and a drift refresh keeps the attestation's `engine`. Fix the matching \"Why\" bullet. Add a dated line to the 2026-11-13 amendment.\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing the engine\": add 1 sentence saying the same, and that changing the plan, or `--force`, which only a human operator uses, makes the next review run afresh.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`: list `currency_basis` and `engine` in `plan_review_status`'s documented return, and regenerate `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json` and `docs/mcp-reference.md` with the repo's existing generators if they embed the text.\n\n## Scope\n- `docs/adr/0123-selectable-plan-review-engine.md`\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json` (regenerated only)\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`: a test pinning the drift-refresh half of the documented behaviour, that a refreshed agentic attestation still reports `engine: \"agentic\"`, if no existing test pins it.\n\nNo config key, environment variable or flag is added.\n\n## Testing\n- RED first: the new or extended test in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py` asserts the documented drift-refresh behaviour. If it already passes, the code already does what the corrected ADR says. Record that on this ticket and keep the test as the pin.\n- `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py tests/interfaces -q` exits 0.\n- `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] ADR 0123 §6 no longer says every shortcut reuses only a pipeline attestation. It states that `idempotent_reuse` and `drift_refresh` act on the current attestation under either engine, and that `verdict_reuse` replays only a pipeline BLOCK.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` §\"Choosing the engine\" states that a pipeline review of an unchanged ticket with a current agentic attestation returns the reused agentic PASS.\n- [ ] The `plan_review_status` tool description in `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` lists `currency_basis` and `engine`.\n- [ ] `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py tests/interfaces -q` exits 0.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"7d68-8e1e-2860-44fc","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"ADR 0123 says pipeline shortcuts reuse only pipeline attestations; they reuse agentic ones"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794590988900953823,"uuid":"9d82ce48-270e-4262-bf0c-9a2514b75983"}